Pushing a new build means uploading a version, then making it live through a deployment. The first step is uploading the version, which workers-versions covers. A deployment is a separate group (workers-deployments). Starting with workers-versions makes sense because the upload comes first and its description says "A version goes live through a deployment."

The wrangler skill could also work if a project config exists, but nothing indicates one does.

